                <pb facs="0149" n="65" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg65"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-06-18"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger, replying to Mr. Hay’s telegram of June 16, reports that he has
                    communicated to the Russian minister the demands of the United States relative
                    to localities to be opened to trade; that the Russian minister says he has no
                    instructions except to await discussion of the question at Washington, and can
                    make no statement to Chinese Government, nor anyone, concerning Russia’s
                    attitude.)</p>
            </div>
